{"schemaVersion":1,"id":"reference:36593a9b05b858cf","name":"Intelligence Officer","source":{"id":"source:reference-36593a9b05b858cf","title":"Intelligence Officer","revision":22569,"timestamp":"2024-09-05T13:47:55Z","sha256":"2426282c7286f8150ef5817bd7a66b9ad3aab57f582dc47f8896991292d18ff0","url":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?oldid=22569","history":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?title=Intelligence%20Officer&action=history"},"article":{"sourceId":"source:reference-36593a9b05b858cf","blocks":[{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"i","children":["Reference Book: ",{"tag":"a","children":["Threats of the Galaxy"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Threats_of_the_Galaxy"}]},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["Intelligence Officers delve into mounds of intercepted codes, plans, and reports to determine the best way to bring down the enemy by knowing more than they do. Handpicked for their natural intelligence and personal charm, Intelligence Officers are masters at teasing out information from a variety of sources. Most are expert interrogators, using a mix of \"carrot and stick\" to cause an enemy agent to spill his guts, revealing vital data or even convincing him to become a turncoat. Although they bear great similarities to ",{"tag":"a","children":["Spies"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Spies"},", Intelligence Officers are part of a strict chain of command and have far more restrictions placed upon them when performing their duties. In short, ",{"tag":"a","children":["Spies"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Spies"}," collect the data and Intelligence Officers process it. \n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["Because of the valuable knowledge they possess, Intelligence Officers are considered key targets and highly sought-after prizes. As a result, they are heavily protected by their units to keep them falling into the hands of the enemy.\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h4","children":["The Chain of Command"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":["An advantage to including an ",{"tag":"a","children":["Officer"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Officer_(CL_8)","referenceId":"reference:cf94f5ed09fd5ba0"},"- as well as a ",{"tag":"a","children":["Commander"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Commander","referenceId":"reference:16af7be312e1840b"}," or a ",{"tag":"a","children":["Commando Squad Leader"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Commando_Squad_Leader","referenceId":"reference:b89fdf754af0b7c7"}," in an encounter is that such a character effectively increases the challenge provided by each individual ally he brings with him. When designing encounters using officers, the Gamemasters should keep in mind that the other enemies in the encounter will be slightly more powerful (though not enough to adjust their CL); although this might not make any difference in an encounter that features only a small number of enemies, the effect becomes cumulative when more enemies are added to the encounter.\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["Each additional enemy is one that is more likely to successfully use the ",{"tag":"a","children":["Aid Another"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Aid_Another","referenceId":"reference:276932074aab1852"}," Action for its allies, causing the heroes' ",{"tag":"a","children":["Defense"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Defense"}," scores to drop while enemy attack bonuses rise. Add to that the Officer's ability to ",{"tag":"a","children":["Share Talents"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Share_Talents"}," (effectively giving ",{"tag":"a","children":["Nonheroic"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Nonheroic","referenceId":"reference:1bca2ef1d9ebe1c3"}," opponents access to abilities usually reserved for heroic characters), and an encounter's difficulty can jump drastically. ",{"tag":"a","children":["Nonheroic"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Nonheroic","referenceId":"reference:1bca2ef1d9ebe1c3"}," enemies under an Officer's command can become tougher to hit and can deal more damage, so Gamemasters who include large numbers of ",{"tag":"a","children":["Nonheroic"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Nonheroic","referenceId":"reference:1bca2ef1d9ebe1c3"}," enemies in an encounter with an ",{"tag":"a","children":["Officer"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Officer","referenceId":"reference:192135a8adabe174"}," should be careful to monitor the effects of an Officer's ",{"tag":"a","children":["Talents"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Talents","referenceId":"reference:e8871b70ebfa07d9"}," on the overall encounter difficulty.\n"]},"\n","\n\n",{"tag":"h3","children":["Intelligence Officer Encounters"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":["Intelligence Officers rarely go into the field on their own- they use the information gleaned by ",{"tag":"a","children":["Spies"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Spies"}," and other sources to make their assessments from the safety of headquarters. Most heroes are likely to encounter an Intelligence Officer after they have been captured and are undergoing interrogation. Intelligence Officers are smooth operators who rarely get riled up (unless they choose to) and are extremely difficult to intimidate or crack. During such interrogations, two to four ",{"tag":"a","children":["Soldiers"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Soldiers_(CL_2)"}," or a single ",{"tag":"a","children":["Elite Soldier"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Elite_Soldier","referenceId":"reference:4937c2ed96b9fdad"}," accompanies an Intelligence Officer to provide both protection and an intimidation factor.\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["When encountered in the field, Intelligence Officers are heavily protected. One might be accompanied by a squad of up to eight ",{"tag":"a","children":["Soldiers"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Soldiers_(CL_2)"},", or a pair of ",{"tag":"a","children":["Elite Soldiers"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Elite_Soldiers"},", as well as a personal ",{"tag":"a","children":["Bodyguard"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Bodyguard","referenceId":"reference:998e41b432f4d199"},". In totalitarian regimes, particularly the Empire, Intelligence Officers might have orders to commit suicide if they are captured, which they carry out after destroying any physical evidence they might possess. In turn, these regimes impose punishment on any troops that kill, rather than capture, enemy intelligence personnel.\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["Intelligence Officers make extensive use of ",{"tag":"a","children":["Droids"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Droids","referenceId":"reference:6e72e583603b9ea8"}," in their work- Protocol Droids for translation and diplomatic situations, Probe Droids for intelligence gathering on far-flung worlds (particularly the ",{"tag":"a","children":["Viper-Series Probe Droid"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Viper-Series_Probe_Droid","referenceId":"reference:80ebc1ca754e6229"},"), and specially designed Interrogation Droids.\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h2","children":["Intelligence Officer Statistics (CL 10)"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":["Medium ",{"tag":"a","children":["Noble"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Noble","referenceId":"reference:190d375ec3483f8f"}," 7/",{"tag":"a","children":["Officer"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Officer","referenceId":"reference:192135a8adabe174"}," 3\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Force Points"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Force_Points"},":"]}," 3\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Initiative"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Initiative","referenceId":"reference:3e687de48a6ad4e5"},":"]}," +11; ",{"tag":"b","children":["Senses:"]}," ",{"tag":"a","children":["Perception"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Perception","referenceId":"reference:bd18e320a6bb9f53"}," +16\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":["Languages:"]}," Basic, Bocce, Bothese, Durese, High